From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bpereira <bpereira@cloudflare.com>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 00:48:21 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 5/7] Speed up filling blurred rounded rects

Replace the corner p-norm with an optional polynomial approximation and
skip the p-norm outside the corners. The poly-pnorm feature remains off
by default in vello_cpu; hotty-blitz enables it; without it the existing per-pixel formula is preserved.

The fit was reported by kitesurf as less than half an alpha LSB. Hotty
render comparisons of the polynomial path against the exact path found at
most one 8-bit channel level across the shadow fixtures. The original
wide-blur subsampling is omitted: overlapping shadows exceeded that bound.

Co-authored-by: hotty Agent <hotty@neuroplast.io>
